prisma
  model Profile {
    id            String   @id @default(uuid())
    email         String   @unique  // ADD THIS LINE
    full_name     String?
    phone         String?
    address       String?
    role          Role     @default(CUSTOMER)
    // password    String?  // Optional: store hashed password here (not recommended)
    created_at    DateTime @default(now())
    favorites     Favorite[]
    cartItems     CartItem[]
    orders        Order[]
    reviews       Review[]

    @@index([email])  // ADD THIS LINE
    @@index([role])
  }

  3. Important Security Notes:

  For Production, You Should:
  1. Create a separate User table for authentication credentials (don't store passwords in Profile)
  2. Use HTTPS only in production
  3. Set secure cookie flags if using cookies instead of localStorage
  4. Consider refresh tokens for better security
  5. Add rate limiting on auth endpoints
  6. Use environment variables for JWT_SECRET (never commit it)

  Better Schema Approach (Recommended):

  prisma
  model User {
    id        String   @id @default(uuid())
    email     String   @unique
    password  String   // hashed password
    profile   Profile? @relation(references: [id])
  }

  model Profile {
    id     String   @id @default(uuid())
    userId String   // References User.id
    full_name     String?
    phone         String?
    address       String?
    role          Role     @default(CUSTOMER)
    created_at    DateTime @default(now())
    // ... relations

    user   User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
  }
